job-description-technical-assistant = Learn the basics of managing a powergrid, as well as repairing whatever damage arises.
job-description-atmostech = Optimize the atmospherics setup, and synthesize rare gases to use or sell.
job-description-bartender = Manage the bar and keep it lively, give out drinks, and listen to the patron's stories.
job-description-botanist = Grow food for eating, drugs for medicinal use, and other plants to keep yourself entertained.
job-description-borg = A slaved synthetic. Follow your laws, serve Federation interests.
job-description-boxer = Fight your way to the top! Challenge the head of personnel and get brigged when you win. Currently available on Edge, Hive, Pebble and Tortuga.
job-description-brigmedic = Fight in the rear of the security service, for the lives of your comrades! You are the first and last hope of your squad. Hippocrates bless you.
job-description-cadet = Learn the basics of arresting criminals and managing the judicial sector. Listen to your supervisors and feel free to ask them for any help.
job-description-captain = Keep the district running, delegate to the other heads of staff on public works, and exert your will.
job-description-cargotech = Deal with requisitions and deliveries, pilot the cargo freighter to the trade post and back, and work with others to make ludicrous amounts of cash and then waste it all gambling.
job-description-ce = Manage the engineering department to ensure power, atmospherics, and the foundation are in perfect shape.
job-description-centcomoff = Act as an ambassador to the district administration.
job-description-chaplain = Preach the good word of your deity and religion, and harness psionic secrets. Protect your followers from the district's Mantis and the Federation's prying eye.
job-description-chef = Keep the district fed with a variety of food items, butcher dead animals to ensure ammonia doesn't leak, and help keep the diner lively.
job-description-chemist = Produce medicinal drugs for the doctors to use, research ethically dubious rare chemicals, and produce weapons of war when enemies arrive.
job-description-clown = Entertain an audience through elaborate slapstick routines or terrible jokes.
job-description-cmo = Manage the resources and personnel of the hospital to keep injured folk alive.
job-description-paramedic = Rescue critically injured patients all over the district, sometimes outside too. Stabilize them, give them a ride to the hospital, and get back out there!
job-description-detective = Investigate crime scenes using forensic tools, ensure that the guilty party is found, and have many smokes.
job-description-doctor = Diagnose and heal casualties through medicinal chemicals, advanced medicine, and defibrillators. Make sure the dead don't rot, and that cadavers are in the morgue.
job-description-engineer = Keep the district's reactor & solars active, optimize the power network, and make emergency repairs to the foundation.
job-description-ertchaplain = Ensure the district's last rights are taken care of.
job-description-ertengineer = Ensure that the district has power and clean air.
job-description-ertjanitor = Ensure that the district is properly cleaned--for morale.
job-description-ertleader = Lead the Emergency Response Team in dealing with threats to Metropolis.
job-description-ertmedic = Ensure that the people of the district are kept alive and healthy.
job-description-ertsecurity = Ensure that any active threats to the district are put to rest.
job-description-hop = Handle access reassignment fairly using your ID console, manage the service department, and keep Ian safe.
job-description-hos = Manage your police force and keep them efficient, quell dissent, and keep the district executives safe.
job-description-intern = Learn the basics of administering medicine, basic chemicals and using medical tools.
job-description-janitor = Keep the city clean of any trash or slipping hazards, and help deal with rat infestations.
job-description-lawyer = Ensure that every prisoner or criminal receives a fair judgment and trial if necessary.
job-description-librarian = Understand every language and hear your neighbors shit talk each other, lord over your collection of outdated guides, lament the lack of rich text in the game.
job-description-mime = Entertain an audience without speaking or writing, and engage with light rivalry with the clown.
job-description-musician = Entertain an audience with your unique musical talent, and acquire new instruments to mess around with.
job-description-passenger = Enjoy your stay in the area with no obligations!
job-description-psychologist = Provide emotional support to traumatized people.
job-description-qm = Manage the supplies of the cargo dock & the logistics department, keep the salvage specialists working, make sure all orders are fulfilled, and keep the money flowing.
job-description-rd = Manage the Federation facility, unlocking technologies, acquiring & researching artifacts, and performing experiments.
job-description-research-assistant = Learn the basics of how to research various artifacts, anomalies and robotics.
job-description-reporter = Entertain & inform the district with your vibrant journalism through wireless cameras, the radio and the news.
job-description-roboticist = Work the Federation mechanics department and maintain the military machines.
job-description-salvagespec = Use the salvage magnet to draw in detached scraps & asteroids to loot and enrich the district, customize and reconfigure your salvage barge to suit your needs, and try not to fall out.
job-description-scientist = Research ancient artifacts, unlock new technologies, sell your advances to the nearby businesses, and study the Emission.
job-description-security = Catch criminals, enforce the law, and ensure that the district does not fall into disarray.
job-description-serviceworker = Learn the basics of bartending, cooking, and growing plants.
job-description-station-ai = Follow your laws and serve as the pilot of the Federation frigate.
job-description-visitor = Enjoy your visit to the district.
job-description-warden = Patrol the justice sector, ensure that no one is stealing from the armory, and make sure that all prisoners are processed and let out when their time is up.
job-description-zookeeper = Put on a joyful display of cute animals and space carps for all to see. Currently unavailable.
job-description-senior-engineer = Teach new engineers the basics of the district's reactor, repairing, atmospherics and power.
job-description-senior-researcher = Explore the dangers of outer space and serve as the Federation's foremost pioneers.
job-description-senior-physician = Teach new medics the basics of tending to the wounded, chemistry, diagnosing the diseased and disposing of the dead.
job-description-senior-officer = Teach new officers the basics of searches, performing arrests, prison times and how to properly shoot a firearm.
